# Only two kinds of thing stay out of this repository now: a secret, and
# anything git would be storing a second copy of.
#
# The user asked for the whole project to be backed up, so the databases,
# the traces and the QA artefacts are all tracked. They are the system's own
# history - what it was asked, what it answered, what it cost - and that
# history exists on one disk otherwise.

# 1. The secret. A live API key in git history is permanent even after a
#    force-push, and this file is regenerated from the key you hold anyway.
.env
config.local.toml

# 2. Derived from files that ARE tracked, so storing it is storing it twice.
#    .venv is 138 MB of Windows-only binaries that uv.lock rebuilds exactly,
#    and a Windows venv does not run on the Linux box CI uses.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
htmlcov/
node_modules/
package-lock.json
